From: EmuFive <blue0x1>
Date: 2026-11-25
Subject: [PATCH 0044] graphics: run PS5 mesh shaders as compute on PS4 GPUs

The PS4 GPU (Liverpool/Gladius, gfx9) has no mesh or task shaders, so games
that draw with mesh shaders (Invincible VS, many Unreal Engine 5 titles) stop
at "Not implemented (!m_graphics.mesh_shader_enabled)".

When the Vulkan mesh+task features are absent, SetMeshProgramsRunAsCompute(true)
is set and the GS-stage NGG/mesh program is recompiled to a compute shader that
writes vertices and primitives into a buffer, one workgroup per NGG subgroup;
renderDraw then draws from that buffer (dispatch_mesh). Detection and workgroup
sizing use the GS fast-launch bits of VGT_SHADER_STAGES_EN and GE_NGG_SUBGRP_CNTL.

Also adds the frameTrace GPU debug facility used while developing this.

